# Testing

Read `docs/conventions/testing.md`.

- Every task ships tests for new/changed behaviour; a bug fix starts with a failing test.
- Layers: packages → Vitest; API unit → Vitest (`src/**/*.spec.ts`); API e2e → Vitest + supertest
  on real Postgres (`test/**/*.e2e-spec.ts`: status codes, validation, authorization, DB
  constraints); web → Vitest + Testing Library; mobile → jest-expo + RNTL; browser flows →
  Playwright (`apps/web/e2e`, #57).
- Deterministic: no real network (fakes for mailer, Google, storage, push, Telegram), injected
  clock, seeded data. Never `Date.now()` in scheduling code under test.
- Time zones: business logic runs in `Europe/Podgorica`; cover the DST days (last Sunday of March
  and October, e.g. 2026-03-29 and 2026-10-25) whenever local wall-clock time is converted.
- Business-scoped endpoints: e2e proves 404 for non-members, 403 for disallowed roles, and
  rejection of cross-tenant ids (API-STD).
- Concurrency-sensitive code (bookings, invitations, token claims) gets a parallel-requests test.
- e2e isolation: unique suffixes per test file, delete what you created in `afterEach`.
- Never skip, `.only`, weaken or delete a test to make CI green.
